<title>USA: U.S. CFTC says CBOT June soybean review is routine. [CORRECTED 22:34 GMT]</title>
<headline>U.S. CFTC says CBOT June soybean review is routine. [CORRECTED 22:34 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Futures Trading Commission, which oversees U.S. futures trading, is making a routine review of price activity and movement during June soybean trading at the Chicago Board of Trade, a spokesman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>(Corrects to remove reference to June contract).</p>
<p>&quot;We are looking into price activity and movement&quot; during June on soybeans, the spokesman said, describing it as a &quot;routine surveillance matter.&quot;</p>
<p>The review was disclosed by the National Farmers Union, which said futures prices dropped by 50 cents a bushel after two processors said they would import foreign-grown soybeans.</p>
</text>
